{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And Abraham drew near and said: Will You then sweep away.</b> If you consider this passage you will find that Abraham's thought was that the Holy One, blessed be He, intended to destroy and annihilate everything through the attribute of justice, and from this he said: 'Will You then sweep away the righteous with the wicked? Will You then sweep away and not bear with the place?' And the word תספה is not second person but third person feminine, in the language of (Hosea 14:3): ״כל תשא עון וקח טוב״. Therefore all of Abraham's prayers in this passage were directed to the attribute of justice — as he said, 'Behold now I have taken it upon myself to speak to my Adonai,' and he said, 'Let not my Adonai be angry,' and he said again, 'Let not my Adonai be angry and I will speak just this once.' And since this was Abraham's thought, he began to rebuke the Holy One, blessed be He: 'Far be it from You to do such a thing,' and he mentioned חלילה לך ('far be it from You') twice, corresponding to the two attributes — the attribute of mercy and the attribute of justice. And he said: far be it from You even in the attribute of justice to put to death the righteous with the wicked, for if so it would be as the righteous as the wicked, and choice and service would be nullified, and denial would multiply in the world; far be it from You in the attribute of mercy — all the more so, for You are the judge of all the earth: 'Shall not the Judge of all the earth do justice?' in the manner that we say on Rosh HaShanah: 'And YHWH of hosts is exalted through justice,' and 'the King of justice.' And the Holy One, blessed be He, made known to him that His thoughts are not Abraham's thoughts, but rather He would deal with them through the attribute of mercy — and that is that the Holy One, blessed be He, speaks with him throughout the entire passage in the language of mercy: 'And YHWH said: The outcry of Sodom and Gomorrah,' and 'And YHWH said: If I find in Sodom.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:28.580193139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}